    "question": "Let G be a simple graph with n ≥ 3 vertices. Which condition guarantees that G contains a Hamiltonian cycle according to Dirac's theorem?",
    "options": {
      "A": "Every vertex has degree at least n / 3.",
      "B": "The minimum degree δ(G) is at least n / 2.",
      "C": "The graph is planar and has more than 2n − 4 edges.",
      "D": "G is bipartite and has a perfect matching."
    },
    "correct_answer": "B",
    "explanation": "Dirac's theorem states that if the minimum degree δ(G) ≥ n/2 for a graph with n ≥ 3, then G is Hamiltonian. The other statements are not sufficient.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  },
