    "question": "Which of the following statements about the complement \\(\\overline{G}\\) of a simple graph G with at least two vertices is always true?",
    "options": {
      "A": "If G is disconnected, then \\(\\overline{G}\\) is also disconnected.",
      "B": "If G is connected, then \\(\\overline{G}\\) is disconnected.",
      "C": "If G is disconnected, then \\(\\overline{G}\\) is connected.",
      "D": "If G has a Hamiltonian cycle, then \\(\\overline{G}\\) has an Eulerian circuit."
    },
    "correct_answer": "C",
    "explanation": "A classic result: the complement of a disconnected simple graph with at least two vertices is always connected. The other implications are false in general.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  },
