    "question": "A simple graph G is r‑regular on n vertices. Which arithmetic condition must always hold for such a graph to exist?",
    "options": {
      "A": "r must be a divisor of n.",
      "B": "n · r must be an even number.",
      "C": "r ≤ n − 2.",
      "D": "n must be a prime number."
    },
    "correct_answer": "B",
    "explanation": "In any graph the sum of all vertex degrees equals 2|E|, which is even. For an r‑regular graph the sum is n·r, so n·r must be even. The other conditions are not required.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  },
