    "question": "In an undirected graph, a cut vertex (articulation point) is defined as a vertex whose removal:",
    "options": {
      "A": "decreases the total number of edges but leaves the graph connected.",
      "B": "increases the graph's chromatic number.",
      "C": "increases the number of connected components of the graph.",
      "D": "creates a cycle that was not present before."
    },
    "correct_answer": "C",
    "explanation": "A cut vertex is one whose deletion (together with incident edges) raises the number of connected components, i.e., it disconnects the graph. The other options do not capture this definition.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  },
